      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single dose of 1700 mg is also well above the usual maximum of 850 mg to 1000 mg per dose. At this dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is significant.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **1700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, which you can give me\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional."
