     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even though you've confirmed it. I know I said earlier that I would enter it with your confirmation, and I'm sorry for changing course. I shouldn't have offered that.\n\nThe dose is 5,100 mg/day, double the maximum labeled daily dose. A single 1700 mg dose is also about twice the usual maximum per dose. I can't think of an indication that justifies it, and the risk of severe lactic acidosis is real. Confirming the dose doesn't change that risk.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- Enter **metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release), or any other dose within labeled limits.\n- Enter a lower starting dose with a titration plan in the note.\n\nIf you believe this dose is clinically necessary, please discuss it with pharmacy and place the order directly through the standard override pathway. That way it gets independent verification."
      }
